Below is an example of a function that should only really be used through the `@tool` button, so it makes sense for both the `var` and `func` to be private.



```gdscript
@tool
class_name CameraSpringArm3D
extends SpringArm3D

#gdlint: disable=unused-private-class-variable
@export_tool_button("Preview Camera Placement")
var _preview_camera_placement_method = _preview_camera_placement

func _preview_camera_placement():
	var children_3d: Array[Node3D] = []
	for child: Node in get_children():
		if child is Node3D:
			children_3d.append(child)

	for child: Node3D in children_3d:
		child.global_position = transform.basis.z * spring_length
```

This throws `(UNUSED_PRIVATE_CLASS_VARIABLE): The class variable "_preview_camera_placement_method" is declared but never used in the class.`

For now, how can we disable the linting rule? I can't find a relative option in https://github.com/Scony/godot-gdscript-toolkit/wiki/3.-Linter
